# No "ensure" — forbidden

The word **`ensure`** must never appear in this codebase — not in identifiers, comments, strings, docs, or error messages.

## Do not use

- Function names like `ensureX`, `ensureSomething`
- File names like `ensure-*.ts`
- Comments or prose: "ensure that…", "this ensures…"
- Error messages containing "ensure"

## Use instead

| Instead of | Prefer |
|---|---|
| `ensureReferenceData` | `seedReferenceDataIfEmpty` |
| `ensureWorkspaceForOrganization` | `getOrCreateWorkspaceForOrganization` |
| `ensureOrganizationForUser` | `getOrCreateOrganizationForUser` |
| `ensurePlatformVoice` | `getOrCreatePlatformVoice` |
| `ensureCfBindings` | `initCfBindings` |
| "ensure X is set" (prose) | "confirm X is set", "verify X is set", "X must be set" |

When writing new code, pick a concrete verb: `init`, `getOrCreate`, `seed`, `provision`, `verify`, `require`.

Full project conventions: `.agents/skills/goals-ac-conventions/SKILL.md`.
